# Context filter for `docker build -f hangar-service/Dockerfile .` (context =
# repo root). Docker uses <Dockerfile>.dockerignore instead of the root
# .dockerignore. ALLOW-LIST: ignore everything, re-include only what the image
# needs. The root holds .env files, service-account keys and private org guides,
# and the image may be pushed to a public registry -- never widen this lightly.
*

!hangar-service/requirements.txt
!hangar-service/src/**
!hangar-editor/**

# ...but never these, even inside the re-included trees.
hangar-editor/node_modules
hangar-editor/dist
hangar-editor/coverage
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env*
**/*key*.json
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/credentials.json
OrgGuides
**/OrgGuides
